      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Three hundred three patients who underwent off-pump coronary bypass were compared with 483 patients who underwent standard on-pump coronary bypass. There was a significant reduction in intraoperative blood transfusion requirements, as well as a significant reduction in the incidence of neurologic, renal, and prolonged ventilatory complications in the off-pump group."},
